{"content":[{"c":["SHELEMIAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Korahite from the tribe of Levi and a gatekeeper who was chosen by lot to guard the east gate of the sanctuary during David’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.26.14","r":"1Chr.26.14","rawR":"1Chr.26.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.26.14","value":"1Chr.26.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 26:14"},"); also named Meshelemiah (vv ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.26.1-2","r":"1Chr.26.1-2","rawR":"1Chr.26.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.26.1-2","value":"1Chr.26.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"1-2"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Meshelemiah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Meshelemiah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Meshelemiah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Meshelemiah"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2–3. Two of Binnui’s sons, who were encouraged to divorce their foreign wives during Ezra’s postexilic reforms in Israel (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.39-41","r":"Ezra.10.39-41","rawR":"Ezra.10.39-41","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.39-41","value":"Ezra.10.39-41"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:39-41"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Father of Hananiah. Hananiah repaired a section of the Jerusalem wall under Nehemiah (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.30","r":"Neh.3.30","rawR":"Neh.3.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.30","value":"Neh.3.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:30"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. Priest and one of the three men appointed by Nehemiah as the treasurers of the temple in Jerusalem. Their task was to oversee the distribution of the tithes among their fellow priests (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.13.13","r":"Neh.13.13","rawR":"Neh.13.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.13.13","value":"Neh.13.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 13:13"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["6. Son of Cushi, the father of Nethaniah, and a forefather of Jehudi (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.36.14","r":"Jer.36.14","rawR":"Jer.36.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.36.14","value":"Jer.36.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 36:14"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["7. Son of Abdeel who, with Jerahmeel and Seraiah, was commanded by King Jehoiakim of Judah (609–598 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},") to seize Baruch and Jeremiah (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.36.26","r":"Jer.36.26","rawR":"Jer.36.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.36.26","value":"Jer.36.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 36:26"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["8. Father of Jehucal (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.37.3","r":"Jer.37.3","rawR":"Jer.37.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.37.3","value":"Jer.37.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 37:3"},"), alternately spelled Jucal in ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.38.1","r":"Jer.38.1","rawR":"Jer.38.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.38.1","value":"Jer.38.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"38:1"}," (",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," mg)."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["9. Son of Hananiah and the father of Irijah. Irijah arrested Jeremiah for apparently deserting to the Babylonians (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.37.13","r":"Jer.37.13","rawR":"Jer.37.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.37.13","value":"Jer.37.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 37:13"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Shelemiah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 26:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.26.14","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.26.14","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.26.14"},{"anchorText":"1-2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.26.1-2","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.26.1-2","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.26.1-2"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 10:39-41","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.10.39-41","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.10.39-41","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.10.39-41"},{"anchorText":"Neh 3:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.3.30","rawQueryValue":"Neh.3.30","sourceRefExact":"Neh.3.30"},{"anchorText":"Neh 13:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.13.13","rawQueryValue":"Neh.13.13","sourceRefExact":"Neh.13.13"},{"anchorText":"Jer 36:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.36.14","rawQueryValue":"Jer.36.14","sourceRefExact":"Jer.36.14"},{"anchorText":"Jer 36:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.36.26","rawQueryValue":"Jer.36.26","sourceRefExact":"Jer.36.26"},{"anchorText":"Jer 37:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.37.3","rawQueryValue":"Jer.37.3","sourceRefExact":"Jer.37.3"},{"anchorText":"38:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.38.1","rawQueryValue":"Jer.38.1","sourceRefExact":"Jer.38.1"},{"anchorText":"Jer 37:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.37.13","rawQueryValue":"Jer.37.13","sourceRefExact":"Jer.37.13"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"badb55ec1e6f1c24b0e45ea88ddea38c233fdd928c49e2f7297d4e91f544e871","sourceItemName":"Shelemiah","sourceItemOrder":260,"sourceMember":"Articles/S.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Shelemiah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Shelemiah","title":"Shelemiah","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}